# Commits that touched formatting only, and should not own a line in `git blame`.
#
# GitHub's blame view reads this file automatically. Locally it does nothing
# until you opt in, once per clone:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add a commit here if it changed no behaviour. The test is mechanical: the
# commit must be empty under `git show --ignore-cr-at-eol <sha>` (for line-ending
# changes) or `git show -w <sha>` (for whitespace). A commit that also moved code
# does not belong here — blame would then skip a real change, which is worse than
# the noise this file exists to remove. Full 40-character SHAs only; git rejects
# abbreviated ones.

